roven decision quality and technical competence, while B lacks decision quality evidence. She might still recommend C, but note that we need more info on crew cooperation and adaptability.\n\nThus Sarah's public message: \"I agree with Emily that C's decision quality and stress resilience are strong, and James just confirmed technical competence. However, we still lack evidence on attention to detail and adaptability; but given the critical nature of decision-making, I still recommend C, pending further discussion on crew cooperation.\" Vote C.\n\nLet's craft."}
